    "raw_answer": "To determine the relative direction of the door from your position at the window while facing the telephone, we can project the coordinates onto a 2D horizontal plane $(x, y)$:\n\n* **Window (Your Position):** $(0.1, 5.0)$\n* **Telephone (Facing Direction):** $(4.2, 4.8)$\n* **Door:** $(9.9, 1.5)$\n\nNext, we calculate the vectors from your position (the window):\n* **Facing Vector (to Telephone):** $\\vec{V}_{\\text{facing}} = (4.2 - 0.1, 4.8 - 5.0) = (4.1, -0.2)$\n* **Door Vector (to Door):** $\\vec{V}_{\\text{door}} = (9.9 - 0.1, 1.5 - 5.0) = (9.8, -3.5)$\n\nNow, we find the angle of each vector relative to the positive x-axis:\n* **Facing Angle:** $\\theta_{\\text{facing}} \\approx -2.8^\\circ$ (almost straight ahead along the positive x-axis)\n* **Door Angle:** $\\theta_{\\text{door}} \\approx -19.6^\\circ$\n\nThe relative angle of the door to your facing direction is:\n$$\\theta_{\\text{door}} - \\theta_{\\text{facing}} \\approx -19.6^\\circ - (-2.8^\\circ) = -16.8^\\circ$$\n\nA negative angle indicates a clockwise direction, which corresponds to your **right**. Since the angle is only $16.8^\\circ$, it is well within the range of being to your right (and not to your back).\n\nANSWER: B",
